# Display Subtasks on Task Card

## Goal Description
Display the number of completed subtasks vs total subtasks on the task card in the project board. This provides a quick overview of task progress without opening the detail modal.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> This change involves modifying the backend API to return subtask counts and updating the frontend to render this information.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend
#### [MODIFY] [TaskController.cs](file:///d:/GITHUB/DACN_ProjectManagement/ProjectManagement/Controllers/TaskController.cs)
- Update [List](file:///d:/GITHUB/DACN_ProjectManagement/ProjectManagement/Controllers/TaskController.cs#142-178) method to include `SubTaskCount` and `CompletedSubTaskCount` in the returned JSON.
- Update [Get](file:///d:/GITHUB/DACN_ProjectManagement/ProjectManagement/Controllers/TaskController.cs#179-218) method (optional but recommended) to include subtask counts for consistency.

### Frontend
#### [MODIFY] [taskUI.js](file:///d:/GITHUB/DACN_ProjectManagement/ProjectManagement/wwwroot/js/taskUI.js)
- Update [createTaskCardHtml](file:///d:/GITHUB/DACN_ProjectManagement/ProjectManagement/wwwroot/js/taskUI.js#24-93) function to accept and render subtask progress.
- Add an icon (e.g., check-square) and text (e.g., "1/3") to the task card footer, alongside comment and attachment counts.
- Only display if `SubTaskCount > 0`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- None planned for this specific UI feature.

### Manual Verification
1.  **Backend**:
    -   Use Swagger or Browser to call `/boards/{boardId}/columns/{columnId}/tasks` and verify the response contains `subTaskCount` and `completedSubTaskCount`.
2.  **Frontend**:
    -   Reload the project board.
    -   Verify that tasks with subtasks show the progress indicator (e.g., "1/3").
    -   Verify that tasks without subtasks do not show the indicator.
    -   Add/Delete/Complete subtasks in the modal and verify the card updates (might need page reload or additional event handling if we want real-time updates without reload - for now, reload is acceptable, or we can update the DOM element if we have time).
